comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T23:19:18.831Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: searched all statuses for the exact dependency names and current outdated inventory. Historical refreshes are terminal; pm-r31390, pm-do5b, and pm-ksr40d remain the canonical disposition records for incompatible candidates. This item owns only the two newly available compatible patches."
  "2026-07-29T00:42:32.105Z","harness:codex","Verification note: the production audit linked test passed. A nested pnpm test:coverage run under pm test failed because the linked-test sandbox deliberately injects an outer PM_PATH and broad root-fixture ownership tests then observe the sandbox tracker. This is harness-context contamination rather than a product failure; the unsafe recursive link was removed and the complete suite is rerun directly from the repository root."
  "2026-07-29T01:01:42.876Z","harness:codex","Delivery evidence: adopted compatible @types/node 26.1.2 and jscpd 5.0.14 patches, refreshed the lockfile, and burned the ESLint suppression ceiling from 131 to 130. Production audit reports no vulnerabilities. Sentry 10.68 remains rejected by closed pm-r31390, TypeScript 7 remains on pm-do5b, and npm-package-arg 14 remains on pm-ksr40d because their live compatibility evidence is unresolved. Final direct coverage passed 6,497 tests at exact 100/100/100/100."
